---
// Needs you: the Overseer page as captured (asked what needs you, it asks with a card before
// archiving), and beside it an illustration of the same news on a phone's lock screen as a push.
// A browser can't capture a lock screen, so that phone is drawn, and says so to assistive tech.
// The phone stands beside the screenshot, never over it, and its lock screen is drawn at a real
// phone's proportions (styles: .lock in site.css).
import Mark from "../Mark.astro";
import ScreenFrame from "./ScreenFrame.astro";
---
<figure class="ovs">
  <ScreenFrame at="feature.overseer" class="ovs-desk" />
  <div class="lock" role="img" aria-label="Illustration: a phone's lock screen with 2 Sova notifications, one for a session that needs input and one for a session that stopped with an error.">
    <div class="lock-screen" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="lock-status"><span>Sat</span><span>84%</span></div>
      <div class="lock-time">9:41</div>
      <div class="lock-date">Saturday, October 10</div>
      <div class="lock-list">
        <div class="lock-notif">
          <Mark tile size={20} class="lock-icon" />
          <div class="lock-text">
            <div class="lock-top"><span class="lock-app">Sova</span><span>now</span></div>
            <div class="lock-title">Needs input · Upload metrics</div>
            <div class="lock-body">A part can fail and then succeed on a retry. Does that count as a failure?</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lock-notif">
          <Mark tile size={20} class="lock-icon" />
          <div class="lock-text">
            <div class="lock-top"><span class="lock-app">Sova</span><span>14m ago</span></div>
            <div class="lock-title">Error · Flaky upload test</div>
            <div class="lock-body">The last turn stopped with an error.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</figure>
